+## GW1a pins (docs/animation/pending/gw1a-pins/README.md). Main's data now carries the 9 November switches, and seven of these tests stage a body or a hold by hand on the way the game played BEFORE one of them: each of those
+## tests holds that one switch OFF for its own run and puts it back after (an in-place edit of the loaded row or the tools' own setter, never a data file), and says why here. The ON path is covered by its own rows
+## (the water floor's ON path is `_test_water_stance`; the flight strikes' own rows wait in the flight-strikes park; the grapple director ON has no row here, it is read in live matches and by the grip clips).
+##   water floor (`WorldFill.setFloor`): the slope row digs a crater and the follow-through and solve-carry rows hold a body at y = 0 over deep sea, and each measures the motion of a body on dry ground or in the air. With the
+##   floor ON (and water v2's fill and the director's water on with it: any one of the three off puts the row right again) the crater is flooded and the sea is a floor, so that body stands on the water (the slope row's ankles are
+##   a water depth off the ground, the others' pelvis steps are the standing body's), another stance than the rows were written for.
+##   grapple director (`grapple.enabled` in data/director/interrupts.json, `DirGrapple.on`): the grip-feed and grip-throw rows feed a hold into `AnimFighter._feed_from` BY HAND (the seam the tests have) while the sim
+##   holds no grapple; with the director ON the live feed (`AnimFighter._feed`) runs every frame, reads "no grapple" from `DirGrapple.now` and ends the hold the test just fed, so no stage ever shows.
+##   flight strikes (`DirZip.setFsForce`): the zip-view rows start a plain zip by `DirZip.start` and an AI exit; with flight strikes ON the zip is the one grammar of paths read from the left stick and the staged exit
+##   is not the path's, so every exit comes out "home".
+##   globe ground (`RenderTileGround.on`, the default since Orb's decision 3 of 2026-11-13): the water-stance row picks a sea cell out of `S.water`, and on the globe ground the match is a planet slice whose `S.water` is all zero
+##   (the sea lives in the tile field), so the row finds no water and stands nobody on it. It runs on the strip ground, the world it reads the sim's water from; the globe ground's own stance on water has no row yet.
+func _pin_floor_off() -> bool:
+	var was: bool = WorldFill.floorOn()
+	WorldFill.setFloor(false)
+	return was
+
+
+func _pin_floor_restore(was: bool) -> void:
+	WorldFill.setFloor(was)
+
+
+func _pin_grapple_off() -> bool:
+	var g: Dictionary = DirGrapple.cfg()
+	var was: bool = bool(g.get("enabled", false))
+	g["enabled"] = false
+	return was
+
+
+func _pin_grapple_restore(was: bool) -> void:
+	DirGrapple.cfg()["enabled"] = was
+
+
+func _pin_flight_strikes_off() -> int:
+	DirZip.setFsForce(0)
+	return -1
+
+
+func _pin_flight_strikes_restore(was: int) -> void:
+	DirZip.setFsForce(was)
+
+
+func _pin_strip_ground() -> bool:
+	var was: bool = RenderTileGround.on
+	RenderTileGround.on = false
+	return was
+
+
+func _pin_strip_ground_restore(was: bool) -> void:
+	RenderTileGround.on = was
+
+
+func _test_slope() -> void:
+	var pin := _pin_floor_off()
+	_test_slope_run()
+	_pin_floor_restore(pin)
+
+
+func _test_follow_through() -> void:
+	var pin := _pin_floor_off()
+	_test_follow_through_run()
+	_pin_floor_restore(pin)
+
+
+func _test_solve_carry() -> void:
+	var pin := _pin_floor_off()
+	_test_solve_carry_run()
+	_pin_floor_restore(pin)
+
+
+func _test_grip_feed() -> void:
+	var pin := _pin_grapple_off()
+	_test_grip_feed_run()
+	_pin_grapple_restore(pin)
+
+
+func _test_grip_throw() -> void:
+	var pin := _pin_grapple_off()
+	_test_grip_throw_run()
+	_pin_grapple_restore(pin)
+
+
+func _test_zip_view() -> void:
+	var pin := _pin_flight_strikes_off()
+	_test_zip_view_run()
+	_pin_flight_strikes_restore(pin)
+
+
+func _test_water_stance() -> void:
+	var pin := _pin_strip_ground()
+	_test_water_stance_run()
+	_pin_strip_ground_restore(pin)
+
